R1 F16 (colour range) - done 2026-10-28
- frame_to_bgr honours FrameMeta::color_range (T2's additive field, types.hpp ColorRange): kFull -> JFIF conversion
  identical to libjpeg's decoder; kLimited -> OpenCV COLOR_YUV2BGR_NV12 / YUYV (unchanged); kUnknown -> limited +
  process-wide counter + one spdlog warning. Applies to NV12 and YUYV; BGR/RGB/GRAY/JPEG unaffected.
- NEW header rig/imageprep/color.hpp + common/imageprep/color.cpp: nv12_full_range_to_bgr (libjpeg-turbo jdsample.c
  h2v2_fancy_upsample + jdmainct.c edge-row replication + jdcolor.c integer tables), yuyv_full_range_to_bgr (tables,
  sample replication), frame_to_bgr_unknown_range_count().
- tests/imageprep/test_color.cpp (libjpeg raw API in the test):
  * full vs cv::imdecode of a JPEG whose own decoded planes (raw_data_out) are the NV12: BIT-EXACT (2 real crops);
  * full vs JPEG encoded from the same NV12 with libjpeg raw_data_in (recorder path; ISP-like planes = BGR2YCrCb +
    2x2 INTER_AREA chroma): measured q100 max 3 / mean 0.15, q90 max 19 / mean 1.2 LSB; asserted q100 max <= 4,
    mean <= 0.3; q90 max <= 32, mean <= 2.0 (DCT loss only). Limited conversion of the same planes: mean ~11, max ~52;
  * limited bit-identical to cvtColorTwoPlane; unknown == limited and increments the counter; gray/primaries.
- Letterbox / remap goldens unchanged and green.
- tests/imageprep/golden_util.cpp: under __SANITIZE_ADDRESS__ adds __lsan_default_suppressions "leak:libtbb.so"
  (system OpenCV's TBB pool intermittently leaves ~12 KB at exit; stack entirely in libtbb).
- For T5 (RawWriter): encode with libjpeg raw_data_in from the full-range NV12 planes, 4:2:0, JFIF; then
  decode == frame_to_bgr(kFull) up to the DCT loss above. Do not convert to BGR first.

