Decisions + contract notes
- No frozen public declaration changed. Private members added to PinholeRadtan (r_valid_) and KannalaBrandt4
  (theta_valid_), and their private constructors take them (header: private members belong to T4).
- New header rig/camera_model/coverage.hpp (own module).
- fov_max_deg: KB4 theta_max = fov/2 (0 -> 89 deg, the Python default); radtan r cap = min(tan 89 deg, tan(fov/2));
  DS/EUCM/VirtualPinhole: ray angle <= fov/2. KB4/radtan/pinhole fov must be < 180, DS/EUCM < 360.
- VirtualPinhole::project does NOT require in-image (Python does, camera_model.py:372); remap/coverage use the Python
  bilinear-safe [0, W-1] rule. Invalid map value -16 (camera_model.py:36).
- scaled() returns nullptr for a non-uniform scale (Python raises); half-pixel convention camera_model.py:42-44.
- EUCM valid set: den > 0 and, for alpha > 0.5, z/den >= (alpha-1)/(2alpha-1) (reduces to the UCM rule at beta=1).
- FIX found by the tests: copyMakeBorder on a ROI pads with the parent's pixels unless BORDER_ISOLATED; numpy views
  never carry a parent, so letterbox uses BORDER_CONSTANT | BORDER_ISOLATED.
- Colour: iPhUMI decodes mp4 with PyAV rgb24 and stores RGB unswapped (gen_replay_buffer_zarr.py:577-603). Rig
  images are BGR, so iPhUMI-layout zarr images need swap_rb=true. frame_to_bgr NV12 = OpenCV COLOR_YUV2BGR_NV12
  (BT.601 limited range); JPEG = cv::imdecode (JFIF full range).
- gen_golden.py writes floats with repr(float(v)) (numpy 2 repr prints 'np.float64(..)'); C++ reads tokens via strtod
  (libstdc++ >> rejects 'nan'). Image goldens are FNV-1a-64 hashes.
- TSan: the tests/imageprep helper sets cv::setNumThreads(0) under __SANITIZE_THREAD__ (system OpenCV is not
  instrumented, so its pool gives false races) and suppresses only `deadlock:libgdal.so` (Ubuntu's OpenCV imread
  loads GDAL, whose CPL mutexes report an inversion inside libgdal).

